            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0521" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.01/37: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-07T14:00:00-07:00">January 7, 1931—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:18 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Your 3, January 6, 6 p.m. Subject to your approval, I propose to answer the
                    Foreign Office note notifying me of the changes in the Government in the
                    following form. First acknowledge in detail the items of the note and then as
                    follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“This information was communicated to my Government and I am now in
                            receipt of instructions to inform Your Excellency that my Government
                            recognizes the change in the Presidency of the Republic and hopes to
                            continue with the Government of Provisional President Reina Andrade the
                            same cordial relations as existed with the Government of President
                            Chacon.[”]</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
